{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness","title":"prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.md","line":822,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.tex#prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-local-isometry]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#cor:pet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.tex","label":"prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness","line":1853,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[uniqueness of Riemannian isometries]\n  \\label{prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0214}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch5-local-isometry, prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties, cor:pet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact}\n\n  \\dcref{ch5:5.6.2}\n  Let $F,G:(M,g_M)\\to(N,g_N)$ be local Riemannian isometries, $M$ connected. If\n  $F(p)=G(p)$ and $DF_p=DG_p$ for some $p\\in M$, then $F=G$ on $M$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\uses{prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness,prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties,cor:pet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact}\n  \\sketch\n  Let $A=\\{x\\mid F(x)=G(x),\\ DF_x=DG_x\\}$.  It is closed and contains $p$.  If\n  $x\\in A$, part (2) of \\cref{prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties} gives\n  \\[\n    F\\circ\\exp_x(v)=\\exp_{F(x)}\\circ DF_x(v)=\\exp_{G(x)}\\circ DG_x(v)=G\\circ\\exp_x(v),\n  \\]\n  The image of a small ball under $\\exp_x$ is a neighborhood by\n  \\cref{cor:pet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact}, so $F=G$ near $x$ and their\n  differentials agree there.  Thus $A$ is open, and connectedness gives $A=M$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[uniqueness of Riemannian isometries] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a7065742d6368352d69736f6d657472792d756e697175656e657373\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0214</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23def%3Apet-ch5-local-isometry\">↗ def:pet-ch5-local-isometry</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23prop%3Apet-ch5-local-isometry-properties\">↗ prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23cor%3Apet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact\">↗ cor:pet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch5:5.6.2</span></span>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F,G:(M,g_M)\\to (N,g_N)$\">$F,G:(M,g_M)\\to (N,g_N)$</span> be local Riemannian isometries, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> connected. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F(p)=G(p)$\">$F(p)=G(p)$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$DF_p=DG_p$\">$DF_p=DG_p$</span> for some <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F=G$\">$F=G$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23prop%3Apet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness\">↗ prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23prop%3Apet-ch5-local-isometry-properties\">↗ prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23cor%3Apet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact\">↗ cor:pet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact</a> \\sketch Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$A=\\{ x\\mid F(x)=G(x),\\  DF_x=DG_x\\} $\">$A=\\{ x\\mid F(x)=G(x),\\  DF_x=DG_x\\} $</span>. It is closed and contains <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span>. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x\\in A$\">$x\\in A$</span>, part (2) of <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23prop%3Apet-ch5-local-isometry-properties\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a7065742d6368352d6c6f63616c2d69736f6d657472792d70726f70657274696573\">subsection 6.1</a> gives </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  F\\circ \\exp _x(v)=\\exp _{F(x)}\\circ DF_x(v)=\\exp _{G(x)}\\circ DG_x(v)=G\\circ \\exp _x(v),  \\]\">\\[  F\\circ \\exp _x(v)=\\exp _{F(x)}\\circ DF_x(v)=\\exp _{G(x)}\\circ DG_x(v)=G\\circ \\exp _x(v),  \\]</span></p><p> The image of a small ball under <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _x$\">$\\exp _x$</span> is a neighborhood by <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23cor%3Apet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#cor:pet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-636f723a7065742d6368352d756e69666f726d2d696e6a65637469766974792d7261646975732d636f6d70616374\">item 2</a>, so <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F=G$\">$F=G$</span> near <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span> and their differentials agree there. Thus <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$A$\">$A$</span> is open, and connectedness gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$A=M$\">$A=M$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#rem:pet-ch5-exp-naturality-intrinsic","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-covering-completeness","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-local-isometry","title":"def:pet-ch5-local-isometry","label":"def:pet-ch5-local-isometry"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties","title":"prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties","label":"prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#cor:pet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact","title":"cor:pet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact","label":"cor:pet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness","title":"prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness","label":"prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness","title":"prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness","label":"prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#thm:pet-ch5-monodromy-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch5-monodromy-theorem","label":"thm:pet-ch5-monodromy-theorem"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#rem:pet-ch5-ex-32","title":"rem:pet-ch5-ex-32","label":"rem:pet-ch5-ex-32"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#rem:pet-ch5-ex-39","title":"rem:pet-ch5-ex-39","label":"rem:pet-ch5-ex-39"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness","title":"prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[uniqueness of Riemannian isometries]\n  \\label{prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0214}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch5-local-isometry, prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties, cor:pet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact}\n\n  \\dcref{ch5:5.6.2}\n  Let $F,G:(M,g_M)\\to(N,g_N)$ be local Riemannian isometries, $M$ connected. If\n  $F(p)=G(p)$ and $DF_p=DG_p$ for some $p\\in M$, then $F=G$ on $M$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\uses{prop:pet-ch5-isometry-uniqueness,prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties,cor:pet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact}\n  \\sketch\n  Let $A=\\{x\\mid F(x)=G(x),\\ DF_x=DG_x\\}$.  It is closed and contains $p$.  If\n  $x\\in A$, part (2) of \\cref{prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties} gives\n  \\[\n    F\\circ\\exp_x(v)=\\exp_{F(x)}\\circ DF_x(v)=\\exp_{G(x)}\\circ DG_x(v)=G\\circ\\exp_x(v),\n  \\]\n  The image of a small ball under $\\exp_x$ is a neighborhood by\n  \\cref{cor:pet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact}, so $F=G$ near $x$ and their\n  differentials agree there.  Thus $A$ is open, and connectedness gives $A=M$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-local-isometry","title":"def:pet-ch5-local-isometry","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties","title":"prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#cor:pet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact","title":"cor:pet-ch5-uniform-injectivity-radius-compact","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}